WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:48.607
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:48.877 --> 00:50.590
I...

3
00:51.296 --> 00:52.896
really...

4
00:54.716 --> 00:56.718
I like you a lot.

5
00:56.718 --> 00:58.338
Ha Na.

6
00:59.803 --> 01:01.384
[Episode 6]

7
01:44.855 --> 01:46.315
What's going on here?

8
01:58.571 --> 02:00.337
Private lesson?

9
02:01.241 --> 02:02.701
It wasn't a private lesson.

10
02:02.701 --> 02:05.620
We just ran through the script once.

11
02:05.620 --> 02:08.831
What are you doing here?

12
02:13.926 --> 02:15.812
I live here now.

13
02:17.304 --> 02:20.510
Guess I can read with her too.

14
02:20.510 --> 02:22.119
Right?

15
02:31.020 --> 02:32.689
Let's go inside.

16
02:32.689 --> 02:34.132
Yeah.

17
03:05.319 --> 03:06.774
Hey.

18
03:07.390 --> 03:08.787
This...

19
03:11.211 --> 03:12.413
Sorry.

20
03:13.062 --> 03:15.651
- It's okay. - Yeah...

21
03:17.525 --> 03:18.693
Well...

22
03:18.693 --> 03:21.029
Want to go to school together tomorrow?

23
03:21.029 --> 03:22.661
What time's your class again?

24
03:22.661 --> 03:26.244
Well, it starts at nine.

25
03:26.244 --> 03:27.452
Mine too.

26
03:27.452 --> 03:29.829
Then we can go together.

27
03:29.829 --> 03:32.165
Yeah, okay.

28
03:32.165 --> 03:33.434
Okay.

29
03:36.053 --> 03:37.843
This clueless idiot.

30
03:37.843 --> 03:40.012
I'm 34. I've got experience.

31
03:40.012 --> 03:43.510
Let me teach you a thing or two, kid.

32
03:43.510 --> 03:45.678
- Jung Woo Jae. - Yeah?

33
03:45.678 --> 03:46.888
So?

34
03:46.888 --> 03:48.515
What?

35
03:48.515 --> 03:50.642
About earlier...

36
03:50.642 --> 03:52.268
What you wanted to say to me...

37
03:52.268 --> 03:53.853
was that all?

38
03:53.853 --> 03:57.661
Yeah. I think so.

39
03:58.316 --> 04:00.235
But...

40
04:00.235 --> 04:04.426
I haven't done everything I want to do with you.

41
04:06.256 --> 04:08.695
W-What do you want to do?

42
04:19.928 --> 04:21.798
Ha Na?

43
04:21.798 --> 04:23.303
What are you...

44
04:25.525 --> 04:26.965
Ha Na...

45
04:30.187 --> 04:33.518
Ha Na! Ha Na!

46
04:33.518 --> 04:34.966
Ha Na.

47
04:35.645 --> 04:37.477
- Ha Na? - Yes?

48
04:37.477 --> 04:40.045
Are you okay?

49
04:40.692 --> 04:42.752
Yeah. Sure.

50
04:42.752 --> 04:44.320
Why?

51
04:44.320 --> 04:47.146
You called my name.

52
04:51.494 --> 04:54.022
I'm fine.

53
04:54.022 --> 04:56.547
I'm so not fine.

54
04:57.166 --> 05:00.814
You're really okay?

55
05:01.754 --> 05:03.795
You feel kind of warm.

56
05:04.424 --> 05:05.916
I'm fine.

57
05:06.682 --> 05:08.767
I'm disappointed in you, Yoon Ha Na.

58
05:08.767 --> 05:10.296
Experienced, my ass.

59
05:10.296 --> 05:12.789
Why am I so nervous?

60
05:13.734 --> 05:16.227
- Want me to get you some medicine? - No!

61
05:16.227 --> 05:19.543
I'm really fine.

62
05:20.273 --> 05:21.274
Tell me if you feel sick.

63
05:21.274 --> 05:23.151
We can go to the ER, okay?

64
05:23.151 --> 05:24.908
Yeah.

65
05:24.908 --> 05:26.253
Okay.

66
05:27.097 --> 05:28.615
See you tomorrow.

67
05:28.615 --> 05:30.783
Yeah.

68
05:30.783 --> 05:34.495
It's late. Get some rest.

69
05:34.495 --> 05:36.623
Then... I'm off.

70
05:36.623 --> 05:37.819
Okay.

71
05:38.458 --> 05:39.778
Yeah.

72
05:40.835 --> 05:42.129
Yeah.

73
05:42.129 --> 05:44.213
- Okay. - Okay.

74
05:44.213 --> 05:45.417
Yeah...

75
05:46.341 --> 05:48.699
- Nine... - Yeah.

76
05:49.344 --> 05:50.686
Yeah.

77
06:35.056 --> 06:37.250
Come on, Yoon Ha Na.

78
06:37.250 --> 06:40.369
I'm 34! Why is this so hard?

79
06:47.735 --> 06:51.328
I really like you.

80
06:53.141 --> 06:54.659
I...

81
06:54.659 --> 06:56.319
really...

82
06:57.286 --> 06:59.388
I like you a lot.

83
07:03.776 --> 07:05.294
Oh my...

84
07:05.294 --> 07:09.048
It's because he is too cute and too cool.

85
07:09.048 --> 07:10.314
That's all it is.

86
07:10.314 --> 07:12.677
It's his fault.

87
07:12.677 --> 07:14.721
And what was with that move?

88
07:14.721 --> 07:17.239
Seriously, Jung Woo Jae...

89
07:17.239 --> 07:18.719
Beats me.

90
07:21.894 --> 07:25.538
And what's with Lee Hyeong Won?

91
07:25.538 --> 07:27.650
Taking Woo Jae's national team spot wasn't enough?

92
07:27.650 --> 07:30.323
Why does he keep showing up and acting like we're close?

93
07:30.323 --> 07:32.822
What if he takes the audition from him too...

94
07:32.822 --> 07:33.823
No.

95
07:33.823 --> 07:35.863
Absolutely not.

96
07:39.149 --> 07:40.621
[Beast]

97
07:40.621 --> 07:42.874
The phone you have called is turned off.

98
07:42.874 --> 07:44.042
You'll be sent to voicemail...

99
07:44.042 --> 07:45.334
What?

100
07:45.334 --> 07:47.249
Why is his phone off?

101
07:48.337 --> 07:50.289
Seriously.

102
07:52.889 --> 07:54.761
[Hanjin Chicken]

103
07:54.761 --> 07:56.168
Let's drink.

104
07:57.614 --> 07:59.108
What's this?

105
08:01.559 --> 08:02.560
It's crispy.

106
08:02.560 --> 08:04.896
Chewy too. This is really good.

107
08:04.896 --> 08:07.857
It's not that harsh, artificial capsaicin stuff.

108
08:07.857 --> 08:11.506
It's that subtle heat from Cheongyang peppers...

109
08:12.361 --> 08:14.296
This is addictive.

110
08:14.953 --> 08:16.824
Hey, look.

111
08:16.824 --> 08:19.285
Stop eating and listen.

112
08:19.285 --> 08:21.454
Ever since Ha Na started school here,

113
08:21.454 --> 08:25.583
she's been the lead in every Yang Jun Mo film.

114
08:25.583 --> 08:27.460
And everything he made with Ha Na

115
08:27.460 --> 08:29.754
was an official selection at Mise-en-scène.

116
08:29.754 --> 08:32.673
Makers Film went crazy for them too.

117
08:32.673 --> 08:37.059
I don't know if it was some lovers' quarrel,

118
08:37.059 --> 08:39.013
but there was one time...

119
08:39.013 --> 08:41.641
when Ha Na turned down his film.

120
08:41.641 --> 08:44.644
Know what happened to it?

121
08:44.644 --> 08:45.817
What was it called again?

122
08:45.817 --> 08:48.022
See? You can't even remember.

123
08:48.022 --> 08:51.067
That's why Yang Jun Mo can't let her go.

124
08:51.067 --> 08:54.654
Why? Because without Ha Na, it's not a Yang Jun Mo film.

125
08:54.654 --> 08:57.281
How could he not fall for her?

126
08:57.281 --> 08:59.539
- I would too... - How did you even get there?

127
08:59.539 --> 09:01.452
Exactly.

128
09:01.452 --> 09:04.288
Yeah. Guess he would fall for her.

129
09:04.288 --> 09:06.290
So even though every character was different...

130
09:06.290 --> 09:08.709
so Ha Na was always the lead.

131
09:08.709 --> 09:12.886
That's why directing majors don't even hit on her.

132
09:12.886 --> 09:16.038
Everyone assumes Ha Na is Jun Mo's.

133
09:16.038 --> 09:18.305
The more I think about it, the more it pisses me off.

134
09:18.305 --> 09:19.929
Greedy bastard.

135
09:19.929 --> 09:22.056
Am I wrong?

136
09:22.056 --> 09:25.461
I wonder how far those two have gone.

137
09:25.461 --> 09:27.186
Seriously.

138
09:27.186 --> 09:28.809
No way.

139
09:30.324 --> 09:31.530
Wait.

140
09:31.530 --> 09:34.902
I think I heard a rumor like that once.

141
09:34.902 --> 09:36.571
Wow, that explains it.

142
09:36.571 --> 09:39.077
No way.

143
09:39.740 --> 09:41.868
You just ruined my drink.

144
09:41.868 --> 09:43.180
I'll take it.

145
09:43.180 --> 09:44.877
You stormed out too.

146
09:44.877 --> 09:46.336
You know something, huh?

147
09:46.336 --> 09:47.337
What?

148
09:47.337 --> 09:48.374
What is it?

149
09:48.374 --> 09:49.667
Come on, tell us.

150
09:49.667 --> 09:52.170
I lost my temper once,

151
09:52.170 --> 09:54.932
and now you're lumping me in with you?

152
09:54.932 --> 09:57.055
This is so damn annoying.

153
09:57.675 --> 09:59.093
You're talking about me?

154
09:59.093 --> 10:01.345
- Bi Gyeong. - Yes?

155
10:01.345 --> 10:05.266
Know why Ha Na gets cast in all those different roles?

156
10:05.266 --> 10:07.185
Because she can pull them all off.

157
10:07.185 --> 10:10.020
She actually becomes the character.

158
10:11.105 --> 10:13.107
While you're sitting here trashing her,

159
10:13.107 --> 10:15.074
she's probably reading her script.

160
10:15.074 --> 10:17.069
- Hey... - What?

161
10:17.069 --> 10:19.054
That hurt?

162
10:19.675 --> 10:23.278
Ha Na would be pretty pissed if she saw this.

163
10:23.278 --> 10:24.887
You're actors too,

164
10:24.887 --> 10:28.838
yet you're acting as if she got cast for something besides talent.

165
10:28.838 --> 10:30.291
And you're her classmate.

166
10:30.291 --> 10:31.626
So?

167
10:31.626 --> 10:33.294
What do you get out of this?

168
10:33.294 --> 10:39.425
Does putting her down change the fact that you're not as good as she is?

169
10:39.425 --> 10:40.557
Feel better now?

170
10:40.557 --> 10:42.261
Seo Ye Rang.

171
10:42.261 --> 10:44.124
Seo Ye Rang.

172
10:44.124 --> 10:45.395
That's enough.

173
10:45.395 --> 10:47.934
You're the one who looks pathetic right now. You know that?

174
10:47.934 --> 10:49.101
What?

175
10:49.101 --> 10:52.236
Your script didn't pass review, so it never got made.

176
10:52.236 --> 10:55.052
Jun Mo's did and yours didn't.

177
10:55.052 --> 10:56.484
Jealous?

178
10:56.484 --> 11:02.198
So you're writing some story about a director and actress having a dirty affair?

179
11:02.198 --> 11:03.863
And it doesn't even make any sense.

180
11:03.863 --> 11:06.490
- You won't quit, will you? - At least...

181
11:07.376 --> 11:10.706
Jun Mo doesn't screw around when it comes to his work.

182
11:10.706 --> 11:13.876
That's why we're all dying to get into one of his shorts.

183
11:13.876 --> 11:15.839
You all know that.

184
11:21.014 --> 11:22.593
What we're trying to do

185
11:22.593 --> 11:25.596
is tell stories about people's hearts.

186
11:25.596 --> 11:27.932
But with hearts this ugly,

187
11:27.932 --> 11:32.561
how are we supposed to move anyone with our films?

188
11:32.561 --> 11:35.075
Can we stop being so pathetic?

189
11:36.107 --> 11:38.073
Lie down with dogs, wake up with fleas.

190
11:38.073 --> 11:39.146
Remember that.

191
11:39.146 --> 11:40.582
Yes.

192
11:40.582 --> 11:42.080
What's with her?

193
11:42.080 --> 11:43.622
Hey!

194
11:44.413 --> 11:47.569
Seo Ye Rang, you're still awesome.

195
11:55.883 --> 11:57.918
Bitter!

196
11:59.922 --> 12:02.284
Oh, I'm so drunk...

197
12:04.940 --> 12:06.280
No, no.

198
12:06.280 --> 12:07.680
Pull yourself together.

199
12:07.680 --> 12:09.540
Get it together.

200
12:19.572 --> 12:22.242
You're that psycho from before.

201
12:23.821 --> 12:26.435
Eat something. You'll wreck your stomach.

202
12:28.159 --> 12:31.252
I don't take food from suspicious people.

203
12:36.366 --> 12:38.019
Fair.

204
12:43.632 --> 12:45.509
Why are you sitting down?

205
12:45.509 --> 12:47.649
Because I want to stay with you.

206
12:48.797 --> 12:50.585
Are you kidding me?

207
12:56.735 --> 12:58.333
Look closely.

208
13:02.568 --> 13:04.403
What do you think?

209
13:04.403 --> 13:07.907
Still can't tell?

210
13:07.907 --> 13:11.427
Nothing? Your heart's not racing?

211
13:19.710 --> 13:21.712
I have really high standards.

212
13:21.712 --> 13:24.940
Most people don't do a thing for me.

213
13:25.758 --> 13:28.312
I'm seriously drunk.

214
13:30.130 --> 13:32.056
What is this?

215
13:36.185 --> 13:37.958
Boss.

216
13:37.958 --> 13:38.985
Hi.

217
13:38.985 --> 13:40.856
Babe!

218
13:40.856 --> 13:43.569
How'd you get here?

219
13:45.312 --> 13:47.238
- You really are something... - What?

220
13:47.238 --> 13:49.361
You never get tired of me, do you?

221
13:49.361 --> 13:50.703
Never.

222
13:50.703 --> 13:53.160
Every time I see you, I fall for you all over again.

223
13:53.160 --> 13:55.746
14 years and counting.

224
13:55.746 --> 13:56.872
Am I that irresistible?

225
13:56.872 --> 14:00.099
Of course. You think I would choose just anyone?

226
14:03.113 --> 14:04.786
Oh, please.

227
14:05.667 --> 14:09.969
I've only ever lived in a world where I thought falling for me was a given.

228
14:09.969 --> 14:13.167
I never knew a world where you didn't fall for me

229
14:13.167 --> 14:15.869
could feel so strange...

230
14:15.869 --> 14:17.852
And sad.

231
14:19.186 --> 14:21.119
What are you talking about?

232
14:24.108 --> 14:26.742
You're handsome, though.

233
14:26.742 --> 14:27.934
Right?

234
14:27.934 --> 14:30.939
Give it time. Your heart will start racing.

235
14:30.939 --> 14:32.692
When it does, you have to tell me.

236
14:32.692 --> 14:34.928
That you've fallen for me. Promise!

237
14:34.928 --> 14:36.260
What?

238
14:39.206 --> 14:42.196
Aren't you going home? It's late.

239
14:42.196 --> 14:43.848
Hands off.

240
14:44.462 --> 14:46.454
I am.

241
15:00.811 --> 15:02.892
Don't follow me.

242
15:23.523 --> 15:25.586
[Happy Home]

243
15:25.586 --> 15:29.134
Look at me, Boss.

244
15:29.757 --> 15:31.406
It's me.

245
15:32.384 --> 15:33.594
Darn it.

246
15:33.594 --> 15:36.019
Hey! Why didn't you answer yesterday?

247
15:36.019 --> 15:37.688
Don't you knock?

248
15:37.688 --> 15:39.225
Why would I?

249
15:39.225 --> 15:40.651
You...

250
15:44.319 --> 15:46.941
- Do you know Lee Hyeong Won? - What?

251
15:46.941 --> 15:49.057
Who's that now?

252
15:52.071 --> 15:53.759
Oh, Lee Hyeong Won!

253
15:54.423 --> 15:55.741
When you were in my body...

254
15:55.741 --> 15:58.559
that judo thug you competed against.

255
16:01.929 --> 16:04.448
[That Summer, Us]

256
16:59.410 --> 17:01.286
One for me...

257
17:05.394 --> 17:07.229
Fried eggs! Looks good.

258
17:07.229 --> 17:08.314
Want me to flip them?

259
17:08.314 --> 17:09.398
- Want to try? - Yeah.

260
17:09.398 --> 17:10.892
Careful.

261
17:10.892 --> 17:13.067
Thanks. Take care.

262
17:18.389 --> 17:22.952
What a world. The owner delivers sundae-guk in an earthenware pot.

263
17:24.448 --> 17:25.654
Look at this.

264
17:25.654 --> 17:28.702
Nothing beats sundae-guk in an earthenware pot.

265
17:28.702 --> 17:31.337
Compared to soup in a disposable plastic bowl,

266
17:31.337 --> 17:33.842
this is on another level.

267
17:36.175 --> 17:37.571
Oh, man.

268
17:38.563 --> 17:39.784
But...

269
17:39.784 --> 17:43.983
Do places actually deliver sundae-guk in plastic containers?

270
17:44.675 --> 17:47.795
I don't know either.

271
18:01.206 --> 18:02.572
Hey.

272
18:17.216 --> 18:20.440
That diet says you haven't quit judo.

273
18:20.440 --> 18:23.207
Hey, why are you here?

274
18:23.207 --> 18:24.842
Did you screw up?

275
18:25.432 --> 18:26.953
Wait...

276
18:27.976 --> 18:29.744
Did you get cut?

277
18:30.441 --> 18:33.856
I didn't screw up, and I didn't get kicked off.

278
18:35.109 --> 18:36.533
That doesn't make sense.

279
18:36.533 --> 18:39.196
A coach just lets his athlete leave like this?

280
18:39.196 --> 18:41.790
No supervision? Just lets you roam free?

281
18:41.790 --> 18:44.294
No way.

282
18:45.162 --> 18:47.121
It's not neglect. It's trust.

283
18:47.121 --> 18:50.415
Coaches micromanage guys who can't deliver on the mat.

284
18:51.053 --> 18:54.753
I guess medalists really do get special treatment.

285
18:54.753 --> 18:56.964
Look at that confidence.

286
18:56.964 --> 18:59.717
Lee Hyeong Won, you've grown up.

287
18:59.717 --> 19:03.915
I'm so proud of you.

288
19:07.175 --> 19:10.880
But why are you auditioning for a short film?

289
19:13.153 --> 19:14.412
What?

290
19:15.531 --> 19:17.358
You little...

291
19:17.358 --> 19:18.885
Hey.

292
19:18.885 --> 19:20.571
What's your dream?

293
19:21.989 --> 19:25.492
I asked you what your dream is, punk.

294
19:25.492 --> 19:26.493
Get lost.

295
19:26.493 --> 19:27.745
Where are you going?

296
19:27.745 --> 19:29.288
Get lost.

297
19:29.288 --> 19:32.916
Damn, always telling me to get lost.

298
19:32.916 --> 19:34.918
You're on the national team, idiot.

299
19:34.918 --> 19:38.345
You represent Korea, remember?

300
19:38.345 --> 19:39.423
Is this really the time?

301
19:39.423 --> 19:41.216
Is this what you should be doing right now?

302
19:41.216 --> 19:44.261
At a time like this, a short film audition?

303
19:44.261 --> 19:46.294
Unbelievable.

304
19:46.294 --> 19:48.334
Are you that out of touch?

305
19:48.334 --> 19:50.321
Are you that out of touch?

306
19:54.396 --> 19:55.814
Choose.

307
19:55.814 --> 19:57.357
You want to be a national team medalist?

308
19:57.357 --> 20:00.347
Or waste your time elsewhere and end up a miserable twat?

309
20:00.347 --> 20:01.713
Choose.

310
20:01.713 --> 20:05.123
Be a judo player, or end up a miserable twat.

311
20:18.003 --> 20:21.477
Was I too harsh?

312
20:25.260 --> 20:27.930
He didn't even finish his food...

313
20:31.391 --> 20:32.957
Seo Ye Rang.

314
20:34.228 --> 20:37.409
How did you pull off all this on this budget?

315
20:37.409 --> 20:39.792
I'm a producer. It's what I do.

316
20:40.859 --> 20:44.029
You secured Haesol City as our filming location,

317
20:44.029 --> 20:46.698
and Ha Na's family home as our base camp.

318
20:46.698 --> 20:49.243
That freed up some room in the budget.

319
20:49.243 --> 20:54.206
So stop worrying about everything else and focus on directing.

320
20:54.206 --> 20:56.166
I can count on you, Ye Rang.

321
20:56.166 --> 20:57.420
Thanks.

322
20:57.420 --> 20:59.078
Don't mention it.

323
21:01.213 --> 21:03.340
After getting that private coaching,

324
21:03.340 --> 21:05.801
I'd better nail this audition.

325
21:05.801 --> 21:09.596
No. Don't think about doing well. Just do it.

326
21:09.596 --> 21:12.413
How am I supposed to "just do it?"

327
21:15.185 --> 21:17.688
Just pretend they're all me.

328
21:17.688 --> 21:19.682
Everyone out there.

329
21:21.024 --> 21:23.652
Just pretend they're all me.

330
21:23.652 --> 21:25.618
Everyone in there.

331
21:27.614 --> 21:28.876
Okay.

332
21:32.417 --> 21:33.854
Ha Na!

333
21:50.929 --> 21:52.410
You okay?

334
21:54.349 --> 21:57.019
Oh, Jung Woo Jae.

335
21:57.019 --> 21:58.478
That was bold.

336
21:58.478 --> 22:02.181
You really startled me.

337
22:02.181 --> 22:03.776
Cute.

338
22:05.952 --> 22:07.405
Shall we go?

339
22:18.118 --> 22:19.230
My treat.

340
22:19.230 --> 22:21.514
- What do you want? - Anything.

341
22:23.490 --> 22:24.992
Wait.

342
22:25.619 --> 22:28.298
Are those two together?

343
22:32.554 --> 22:34.073
Looks like it.

344
22:35.460 --> 22:37.142
I had no idea...

345
22:37.142 --> 22:41.063
Look at you, watching them like a hawk. Such a director.

346
22:41.063 --> 22:43.023
Was I?

347
22:43.023 --> 22:44.033
Yeah.

348
22:44.033 --> 22:45.505
I thought the audition had already started.

349
22:45.505 --> 22:47.019
Come on.

350
22:47.753 --> 22:49.442
Let's go.

351
23:04.211 --> 23:07.368
Isn't that Ye Rang's car?

352
23:07.368 --> 23:10.300
Who the hell is that getting out of her car?

353
23:10.300 --> 23:11.679
Boss!

354
23:19.525 --> 23:21.964
Why do you keep calling me "Boss?"

355
23:24.606 --> 23:26.168
Give me your number!

356
23:30.123 --> 23:31.736
Let's go.

357
23:35.909 --> 23:38.661
- Come on. - Yeah, coming.

358
23:41.456 --> 23:45.505
I look handsome today... Right?

359
23:46.378 --> 23:47.782
Did her type...

360
23:48.886 --> 23:50.514
change?

361
23:58.483 --> 24:00.417
- Get lost. - Where are you going?

362
24:00.417 --> 24:01.643
It's not over for you yet.

363
24:01.643 --> 24:02.923
There's a repechage.

364
24:02.923 --> 24:06.227
Damn, always telling me to get lost.

365
24:07.065 --> 24:08.275
Choose.

366
24:08.275 --> 24:09.943
You want to be a national team medalist?

367
24:09.943 --> 24:12.446
Or waste your time elsewhere and end up a miserable twat?

368
24:12.446 --> 24:13.527
Choose.

369
24:13.527 --> 24:16.931
Be a judo player, or end up a miserable twat.

370
24:38.500 --> 24:39.814
[That Summer, Us]

371
24:56.246 --> 24:58.444
Private lessons behind my back?

372
24:59.930 --> 25:01.606
Feeling threatened, huh?

373
25:04.503 --> 25:06.384
What?

374
25:06.384 --> 25:10.710
Why do you keep coming at me nonstop?

375
25:10.710 --> 25:12.703
And now Ha Na too.

376
25:18.435 --> 25:22.537
You think I only made the national team because you got hurt, right?

377
25:23.183 --> 25:25.901
You know why I made it?

378
25:25.901 --> 25:27.738
I wanted it more.

379
25:28.683 --> 25:31.101
More than you did.

380
25:33.944 --> 25:35.695
Let's say that's true.

381
25:35.695 --> 25:37.364
Do whatever you want to me.

382
25:37.364 --> 25:38.506
But...

383
25:38.506 --> 25:40.158
leave Ha Na alone.

384
25:40.158 --> 25:42.024
I'm serious.

385
25:42.904 --> 25:45.043
That's your problem.

386
25:45.043 --> 25:49.856
Turns out, it wasn't just the medal that I wanted to take from you.

387
25:49.856 --> 25:52.368
I want her just as badly.

388
26:07.310 --> 26:08.978
Wait.

389
26:12.524 --> 26:15.517
Okay, let's do this.

390
26:15.517 --> 26:20.240
I assume you all know my résumé.

391
26:20.240 --> 26:21.575
All right!

392
26:21.575 --> 26:24.119
The dish you're about to make

393
26:24.119 --> 26:27.542
is the one dessert you'd put out into the world

394
26:27.542 --> 26:30.888
with your hotel's name on it.

395
26:30.888 --> 26:33.044
What matters is...

396
26:33.044 --> 26:35.422
taste, visuals, commercial appeal.

397
26:35.422 --> 26:37.617
Flavor, presentation, marketability!

398
26:37.617 --> 26:41.661
Not one of those can fall short of my strict standards.

399
26:41.661 --> 26:45.974
Only one plate survives.

400
26:45.974 --> 26:49.060
Everything else goes in the trash.

401
26:49.060 --> 26:51.938
You know what I'm saying, right?

402
26:51.938 --> 26:57.285
- You get one shot... - An apron instead of a judo uniform.

403
26:57.285 --> 26:59.578
Ready, go!

404
26:59.578 --> 27:00.954
Start cooking!

405
27:00.954 --> 27:04.333
I used to throw people. Now I'm pounding dough?

406
27:04.333 --> 27:05.823
No way...

407
27:08.670 --> 27:10.450
Terrible!

408
27:11.041 --> 27:12.834
Are you crazy?

409
27:12.834 --> 27:13.835
Sorry?

410
27:13.835 --> 27:16.241
No time! Move!

411
27:17.172 --> 27:18.340
Focus!

412
27:18.340 --> 27:19.721
Just focus!

413
27:19.721 --> 27:21.181
Okay...

414
27:21.181 --> 27:25.657
Mom was right. I can't blow my tuition and get smacked by her too.

415
27:25.657 --> 27:27.078
Let's do this.

416
27:27.078 --> 27:28.975
Cooking is your life!

417
27:28.975 --> 27:32.861
Give it everything you've got!

418
27:38.276 --> 27:40.916
- Look at the food! - Oh, right.

419
27:40.916 --> 27:42.388
Look!

420
27:42.388 --> 27:43.894
Hey! You...

421
27:59.256 --> 28:00.818
This is it.

422
28:37.830 --> 28:39.729
Interesting.

423
28:48.564 --> 28:50.312
Shit...

424
28:50.312 --> 28:52.616
You are a loser!

425
29:04.779 --> 29:06.114
Is this food?

426
29:06.114 --> 29:07.782
Is this food?

427
29:07.782 --> 29:11.655
I can't stop myself! So pissed off!

428
29:27.302 --> 29:28.595
What's this?

429
29:28.595 --> 29:30.613
It's Dujjonku.

430
29:31.353 --> 29:32.707
"Du..." What?

431
29:32.707 --> 29:34.476
Dubai Chewy Cookie.

432
29:34.476 --> 29:36.186
Dujjonku.

433
29:36.186 --> 29:38.980
"Dujjonku..."

434
29:38.980 --> 29:42.503
Pick it up and take a bite.

435
29:43.710 --> 29:45.445
With my bare hands?

436
29:45.445 --> 29:46.738
Yes.

437
29:46.738 --> 29:48.500
Impossible.

438
29:52.869 --> 29:54.808
Oh, the smell.

439
30:06.424 --> 30:09.022
With every bite, it bursts open,

440
30:09.022 --> 30:12.806
revealing that pale green pistachio inside.

441
30:12.806 --> 30:15.141
Unbelievable!

442
30:15.141 --> 30:17.644
And with every bite, that crunch...

443
30:17.644 --> 30:19.938
This is incredible!

444
30:19.938 --> 30:22.732
Oh, fantastic!

445
30:22.732 --> 30:24.318
And while you're eating it...

446
30:24.318 --> 30:29.197
this innovative texture makes you want to pay more for it.

447
30:29.197 --> 30:31.329
That's got serious commercial potential!

448
30:31.329 --> 30:33.137
Very good!

449
30:39.874 --> 30:40.883
Amazing!

450
30:40.883 --> 30:43.356
Bravo! Mamma mia!

451
30:43.356 --> 30:45.991
It tastes like ice cream.

452
30:47.006 --> 30:49.551
This is a dessert revolution.

453
30:49.551 --> 30:52.198
Mr. Yoon Ha Ru.

454
30:52.935 --> 30:54.622
Thank you.

455
30:54.622 --> 30:56.249
Let's give him a hand!

456
30:56.249 --> 30:57.629
Applause!

457
30:58.468 --> 30:59.923
You're the best!

458
31:08.649 --> 31:12.490
Actually, this is for someone.

459
31:12.490 --> 31:13.739
Okay.

460
31:14.449 --> 31:15.934
I don't care.

461
31:21.809 --> 31:23.602
[Auditions for the male lead]

462
31:25.222 --> 31:26.475
[That Summer, Us]

463
31:27.964 --> 31:30.467
Gang Ho got So Hee to safety,

464
31:30.467 --> 31:33.052
and now he has to leave to fight again.

465
31:33.052 --> 31:34.471
Improvise the dialogue.

466
31:34.471 --> 31:36.639
Say your final goodbye to So Hee.

467
31:36.639 --> 31:37.827
Okay.

468
31:53.705 --> 31:55.998
I'll kill them all.

469
31:57.118 --> 31:59.329
Anyone who hurts you...

470
31:59.329 --> 32:02.697
I won't leave a single one alive.

471
32:02.697 --> 32:04.226
Just trust me.

472
32:11.925 --> 32:13.384
I can do better.

473
32:13.384 --> 32:15.067
What are you talking about?

474
32:17.180 --> 32:19.015
Isn't that good enough?

475
32:19.015 --> 32:20.436
Yeah?

476
32:34.392 --> 32:35.624
Go ahead and start.

477
32:35.624 --> 32:36.894
Okay.

478
32:40.537 --> 32:43.314
Just pretend they're all me.

479
32:43.314 --> 32:45.022
Everyone in there.

480
33:15.154 --> 33:17.434
No need to be scared.

481
33:18.832 --> 33:21.119
If you wait for me,

482
33:21.119 --> 33:23.538
I'll come back. I promise.

483
33:23.538 --> 33:25.957
Even if you're in the middle of hell,

484
33:25.957 --> 33:29.278
I'll protect you.

485
33:31.261 --> 33:33.714
Just trust me, okay?

486
34:04.537 --> 34:06.873
So who are you picking?

487
34:06.873 --> 34:10.001
You need to decide, Jun Mo.

488
34:10.001 --> 34:12.337
It comes down to balance.

489
34:12.337 --> 34:13.880
If buzz is 90,

490
34:13.880 --> 34:15.840
acting only needs to be 10 to get funded.

491
34:15.840 --> 34:19.177
What if acting is 90 and buzz is 10?

492
34:19.177 --> 34:20.637
That's a tough sell.

493
34:20.637 --> 34:22.138
Being famous...

494
34:22.138 --> 34:25.099
is a lot more power than you think.

495
34:25.099 --> 34:27.933
We're out of time.

496
34:28.603 --> 34:30.188
Any objections?

497
34:30.188 --> 34:31.803
I do.

498
34:32.440 --> 34:37.070
You all saw a total rookie change the whole room.

499
34:37.070 --> 34:40.406
And we're just throwing away that kind of buzz potential?

500
34:40.406 --> 34:42.768
I agree with that.

501
34:42.768 --> 34:45.671
Yeah, but...

502
34:45.671 --> 34:47.955
Walking away from buzz that dropped right into our laps...

503
34:47.955 --> 34:49.378
Darn it...

504
34:49.378 --> 34:51.376
Almost impossible.

505
34:51.376 --> 34:53.152
Exactly.

506
34:54.045 --> 34:56.172
All right.

507
34:56.172 --> 34:57.840
Why are we making this film?

508
34:57.840 --> 34:59.258
Why?

509
34:59.258 --> 35:00.760
So people will watch it.

510
35:00.760 --> 35:03.513
Who would audiences rather see as Gang Ho?

511
35:03.513 --> 35:06.391
National team star Lee Hyeong Won?

512
35:06.391 --> 35:09.644
Or some nobody named Jung Woo Jae?

513
35:09.644 --> 35:12.154
Isn't the answer obvious?

514
35:12.154 --> 35:14.257
Right. Fame is always a plus.

515
35:14.257 --> 35:16.009
Exactly!

516
35:19.404 --> 35:21.126
I'll make the call.

517
35:30.049 --> 35:32.956
The role of Gang Ho...

518
35:34.961 --> 35:37.130
goes to Hyeong Won.

519
35:37.130 --> 35:40.469
Woo Jae, thank you for all your hard work.

520
36:00.987 --> 36:03.740
This can't be happening.

521
36:03.740 --> 36:05.831
This is driving me crazy.

522
36:10.504 --> 36:12.999
We're in this together now, so let's make it work.

523
36:12.999 --> 36:15.251
I'll do my best.

524
36:15.251 --> 36:16.711
Hey, national team!

525
36:16.711 --> 36:18.463
Your right side really is your good side.

526
36:18.463 --> 36:21.064
- Yeah. - She brought the camcorder?

527
36:21.983 --> 36:23.468
Why'd you take that out?

528
36:23.468 --> 36:24.886
Isn't that Ha Na's bag?

529
36:24.886 --> 36:28.473
We're classmates. What's the big deal if I touch it?

530
36:28.473 --> 36:32.602
On the historic day Hyeong Won landed the role...

531
36:32.602 --> 36:35.772
let's get it on camera.

532
36:35.772 --> 36:37.106
Yoon Ha Na.

533
36:37.106 --> 36:38.232
Ha Na.

534
36:38.232 --> 36:40.390
Say hello to your new co-star.

535
36:40.390 --> 36:41.567
Okay.

536
36:41.567 --> 36:43.078
Congrats. Let's do a good job.

537
36:43.078 --> 36:44.300
Yeah.

538
36:48.786 --> 36:50.745
Ha Na, why won't this turn on?

539
36:50.745 --> 36:51.954
Maybe it's broken.

540
36:51.954 --> 36:53.804
Hey! Why are you touching...

541
37:06.018 --> 37:08.672
Hey, are you okay?

542
37:10.306 --> 37:11.417
Come on.

543
37:11.417 --> 37:14.886
Why make such a big deal out of it?

544
37:15.531 --> 37:17.509
"A big deal?"

545
37:17.509 --> 37:21.859
It didn't even work to begin with.

546
37:21.859 --> 37:25.677
Now you're making me look like some kind of jerk.

547
37:26.767 --> 37:28.658
Shin Bi Gyeong.

548
37:28.658 --> 37:30.407
Apologize.

549
37:30.993 --> 37:33.098
- What? - So being classmates...

550
37:33.098 --> 37:35.873
means you can touch her stuff,

551
37:35.873 --> 37:38.835
but she can't tell you to stop?

552
37:38.835 --> 37:41.587
You should feel embarrassed.

553
37:41.587 --> 37:44.651
So apologize.

554
37:48.980 --> 37:52.232
Sorry, Yoon Ha Na.

555
37:54.439 --> 37:56.887
I'll head out first.

556
37:57.774 --> 37:59.745
Ha Na!

557
38:02.817 --> 38:04.323
Seriously...

558
38:07.539 --> 38:10.238
What's taking her so long?

559
38:14.078 --> 38:15.744
Oh, good timing.

560
38:15.744 --> 38:16.975
Is Ye Rang in there?

561
38:16.975 --> 38:19.917
She is, but... that's not the point.

562
38:19.917 --> 38:21.125
What?

563
38:21.776 --> 38:23.809
- Come with me. - Why?

564
38:24.805 --> 38:26.343
Hyeong Won got it?

565
38:26.343 --> 38:28.342
That crazy bastard.

566
38:28.342 --> 38:31.095
It's like he keeps taking Woo Jae's place.

567
38:31.095 --> 38:33.347
Why does he keep getting tangled up with us?

568
38:33.347 --> 38:35.100
I know.

569
38:35.100 --> 38:37.602
Let's find another way.

570
38:37.602 --> 38:40.527
When did Ye Rang start her agency?

571
38:40.527 --> 38:42.773
Not for a few more years.

572
38:42.773 --> 38:44.214
Right.

573
38:44.817 --> 38:48.154
I'm worried about the camcorder too.

574
38:48.154 --> 38:49.488
The camcorder?

575
38:49.488 --> 38:51.908
Carrying it around in my bag isn't safe either.

576
38:51.908 --> 38:54.493
Bi Gyeong almost broke it just now.

577
38:54.493 --> 38:55.842
What?

578
38:56.562 --> 38:59.123
But we can't leave it at home either.

579
38:59.123 --> 39:00.908
Exactly.

580
39:01.751 --> 39:04.045
I'm so scared.

581
39:04.045 --> 39:07.953
What if we suddenly get thrown into another future again?

582
39:07.953 --> 39:11.815
What if we can't see Woo Jae again?

583
39:12.970 --> 39:14.180
No.

584
39:14.180 --> 39:16.974
As long as we don't drop it, it should be okay.

585
39:16.974 --> 39:20.127
We know for sure how to get back to the past where Woo Jae is.

586
39:20.127 --> 39:22.637
But it's random.

587
39:23.519 --> 39:26.711
It never goes the way we expect.

588
39:36.619 --> 39:37.954
I wanted it more.

589
39:37.954 --> 39:40.747
More than you did.

590
39:40.747 --> 39:44.929
Turns out, it wasn't just the medal that I wanted to take from you.

591
39:47.171 --> 39:50.290
Then that bastard Hyeong Won and Ha Na...

592
40:05.815 --> 40:08.877
Woo Jae, want to get chicken and beer later?

593
40:08.877 --> 40:10.736
I'll bring the beer.

594
40:10.736 --> 40:12.105
Just us two?

595
40:43.993 --> 40:45.504
I'll pick you up later.

596
40:45.504 --> 40:47.216
What time do you get off?

597
40:51.610 --> 40:53.262
- Excuse me. - Yeah?

598
40:53.262 --> 40:56.074
Thanks for earlier.

599
40:56.790 --> 40:58.331
For what?

600
40:58.331 --> 40:59.995
You weren't saying what needed to be said,

601
40:59.995 --> 41:02.705
so I couldn't help saying it for you.

602
41:02.705 --> 41:05.978
Speak up for yourself. Bottling it up will make you sick.

603
41:06.834 --> 41:08.654
Thank you.

604
41:10.767 --> 41:14.717
Jun Mo surprised me, though.

605
41:14.717 --> 41:17.636
I thought he'd pick Woo Jae for sure.

606
41:17.636 --> 41:21.640
I didn't think Jun Mo would get swayed by buzz.

607
41:21.640 --> 41:24.310
Maybe Professor Min got in his head.

608
41:24.310 --> 41:27.980
That's not the Jun Mo I know.

609
41:27.980 --> 41:31.192
We should respect Jun Mo's choice.

610
41:31.192 --> 41:33.912
I'm sure he had his reasons.

611
41:35.404 --> 41:37.386
But you...

612
41:37.386 --> 41:39.620
Are you dating Jung Woo Jae?

613
41:40.242 --> 41:41.911
How did you know?

614
41:41.911 --> 41:43.954
A college romance

615
41:43.954 --> 41:47.146
could give you something to draw on as an actress.

616
41:47.146 --> 41:49.141
Most couples in their twenties break up anyway.

617
41:49.141 --> 41:50.319
You won't marry him.

618
41:50.319 --> 41:53.380
And there's nothing to gain from making it so obvious.

619
41:53.380 --> 41:55.763
- Sorry? - I'm not saying don't date.

620
41:55.763 --> 41:58.725
I'm saying don't leave behind stuff you'll regret as an actress.

621
41:58.725 --> 42:02.272
Like plastering couple photos all over social media.

622
42:02.272 --> 42:03.815
What is with her?

623
42:03.815 --> 42:08.183
Did she already have this much CEO energy back then?

624
42:09.438 --> 42:11.482
It's your call, though...

625
42:11.482 --> 42:15.206
- Just a little advice... - Thank you so much.

626
42:16.200 --> 42:17.695
Sure.

627
42:25.908 --> 42:27.589
That was rough, but fun.

628
42:27.589 --> 42:29.508
- Great work, everyone! - Great work.

629
42:29.508 --> 42:31.216
Let's drink!

630
42:32.336 --> 42:34.569
She's a real star.

631
42:34.569 --> 42:35.840
Hey, she can't drink.

632
42:35.840 --> 42:38.333
Jun Mo, let's get some air. The director can't get drunk.

633
42:38.333 --> 42:39.613
- Shall we get some air? - Let's go.

634
42:39.613 --> 42:40.780
Yeah.

635
42:41.406 --> 42:43.764
Want some ice cream? My treat.

636
42:43.764 --> 42:45.054
- Really? - Yeah.

637
42:45.054 --> 42:46.168
What about Ha Na?

638
42:46.168 --> 42:47.387
Okay.

639
42:57.278 --> 42:58.976
Hey!

640
42:58.976 --> 43:00.359
Yes?

641
43:00.359 --> 43:01.957
Drink with me.

642
43:01.957 --> 43:05.418
Ye Rang, so that's what it was.

643
43:05.418 --> 43:08.005
That's why...

644
43:08.005 --> 43:10.215
You were so good,

645
43:10.215 --> 43:14.170
and no matter how hard I practiced, I couldn't catch up.

646
43:14.170 --> 43:17.089
I was so jealous of you,

647
43:17.089 --> 43:20.593
and I hated myself!

648
43:20.593 --> 43:24.344
I thought you...

649
43:24.344 --> 43:27.641
hated me for no reason.

650
43:27.641 --> 43:29.270
Hey...

651
43:30.769 --> 43:33.272
How could I hate you?

652
43:33.272 --> 43:35.699
You're this pretty and talented.

653
43:35.699 --> 43:38.744
Why would I hate you?

654
43:38.744 --> 43:41.155
Ye Rang, don't cry.

655
43:41.155 --> 43:43.568
You're pretty too.

656
43:44.333 --> 43:46.535
No, no.

657
43:46.535 --> 43:49.580
You're way prettier.

658
43:49.580 --> 43:53.584
No, you're way prettier.

659
43:53.584 --> 43:56.128
Come here, little sis.

660
43:56.128 --> 43:57.692
Ye Rang.

661
44:01.973 --> 44:04.979
- Don't be silly. - Don't cry.

662
44:11.503 --> 44:13.045
I'm sorry.

663
44:13.045 --> 44:16.440
I'm more sorry, dear.

664
44:16.440 --> 44:20.517
Back then, I thought she was just this scary, tough-as-nails senior.

665
44:20.517 --> 44:23.239
Who knew she had this cute side hidden underneath?

666
44:23.239 --> 44:26.005
Should I make the first move this time?

667
44:34.922 --> 44:36.649
Well...

668
44:37.300 --> 44:39.972
Can I call you "unnie?"

669
44:40.654 --> 44:41.481
Sorry?

670
44:41.481 --> 44:44.802
I just think you're so pretty, unnie.

671
44:44.802 --> 44:46.247
Okay, unnie?

672
44:47.810 --> 44:51.267
Sure. Whatever you want.

673
44:51.267 --> 44:52.909
Oh, right.

674
44:52.909 --> 44:56.355
Someone asked me to give you this.

675
44:56.355 --> 44:57.445
Who?

676
44:57.445 --> 45:01.272
My parents' son.

677
45:01.926 --> 45:03.362
"Your parents' son?"

678
45:03.362 --> 45:04.498
My brother.

679
45:04.498 --> 45:05.739
I think he likes you.

680
45:05.739 --> 45:07.713
He made it himself. Dujjonku.

681
45:07.713 --> 45:09.941
"Dujjonku?"

682
45:10.942 --> 45:12.448
Dujjonku...

683
45:19.383 --> 45:21.021
It was nice seeing you this morning, Boss.

684
45:21.021 --> 45:22.431
This is my number.

685
45:22.431 --> 45:26.567
If the Dujjonku is good, text "1." If not, text "2."

686
45:26.567 --> 45:28.137
What is this?

687
45:28.137 --> 45:29.822
See you tomorrow.

688
45:29.822 --> 45:31.609
Oh, okay.

689
45:35.388 --> 45:37.482
How am I supposed to eat this...

690
45:38.605 --> 45:40.206
Dujjonku...

691
45:41.283 --> 45:42.562
Give me your number!

692
45:42.562 --> 45:45.446
Then that total nutcase from this morning...

693
45:45.446 --> 45:46.983
Yoon Ha Ru?

694
45:57.915 --> 45:59.615
[You got a heart] [Check it out now on Jennypang]

695
46:01.374 --> 46:04.058
What the heck...

696
46:16.560 --> 46:18.314
Is it over?

697
46:19.521 --> 46:21.148
Yeah.

698
46:21.148 --> 46:24.528
It's really over, right?

699
46:26.070 --> 46:28.343
No one can find us now.

700
46:32.376 --> 46:34.203
Just one more time.

701
46:36.413 --> 46:38.499
Let's call it a day.

702
46:38.499 --> 46:40.646
We can pick this up tomorrow.

703
46:51.762 --> 46:54.264
I have training tomorrow.

704
46:54.264 --> 46:56.809
Shouldn't we do more tonight?

705
46:56.809 --> 46:59.128
I admire the enthusiasm.

706
46:59.128 --> 47:01.647
But mindless repetition isn't the answer.

707
47:01.647 --> 47:05.067
Right now, instead of getting the lines out of your mouth,

708
47:05.067 --> 47:08.662
you need time to read the script over and over.

709
47:08.662 --> 47:09.738
Keep your lips closed.

710
47:09.738 --> 47:11.995
Read it. Feel it. Think about it.

711
47:11.995 --> 47:13.826
Really put yourself in Gang Ho's shoes.

712
47:13.826 --> 47:16.120
You just don't want to practice with me, do you?

713
47:16.120 --> 47:19.048
I'm just saying, use your enthusiasm...

714
47:20.628 --> 47:22.793
Ye Rang texted me a "1!"

715
47:22.793 --> 47:24.128
Look! "1!"

716
47:24.128 --> 47:25.795
See?

717
47:26.380 --> 47:27.897
Hey! See this?

718
47:27.897 --> 47:29.057
"1!"

719
47:29.057 --> 47:30.283
So proud of myself.

720
47:30.283 --> 47:33.176
See? She sent me a "1!"

721
47:34.248 --> 47:36.139
Oh, this...

722
47:39.551 --> 47:41.100
By the way...

723
47:41.728 --> 47:43.724
What are you doing here?

724
47:55.834 --> 47:58.328
Come here.

725
47:58.328 --> 47:59.438
Are you crazy?

726
47:59.438 --> 48:02.532
What? Just come here.

727
48:03.125 --> 48:04.501
Let go.

728
48:04.501 --> 48:06.931
Come on, you bastard.

729
48:15.429 --> 48:17.245
Want some chicken?

730
48:17.245 --> 48:18.556
Let's eat.

731
48:19.770 --> 48:21.214
I'll open it for you.

732
48:26.703 --> 48:28.358
Is judo a joke to you?

733
48:28.358 --> 48:30.370
You think your spot is secure?

734
48:35.624 --> 48:38.619
When Woo Jae got hurt and you made the national team,

735
48:38.619 --> 48:42.147
everyone ran their mouth about how you got lucky, right?

736
48:42.748 --> 48:44.032
Of course.

737
48:44.032 --> 48:45.959
Just loudmouths talking crap.

738
48:45.959 --> 48:48.170
But I know.

739
48:48.170 --> 48:49.588
Judo doesn't lie.

740
48:49.588 --> 48:50.672
It wasn't luck.

741
48:50.672 --> 48:53.509
All that time on the mat got you on the national team.

742
48:53.509 --> 48:56.099
Sweat on the mat never betrays you.

743
48:56.099 --> 48:58.639
You're the one doing the betraying.

744
48:58.639 --> 49:00.098
Think carefully.

745
49:00.098 --> 49:01.475
About what you really want.

746
49:01.475 --> 49:04.167
Where you really belong.

747
49:06.480 --> 49:08.631
Don't cross the line.

748
49:08.631 --> 49:11.151
You could seriously get yourself killed.

749
49:11.151 --> 49:14.446
What's with that death glare?

750
49:14.446 --> 49:15.995
Who are you threatening?

751
49:15.995 --> 49:20.371
I'm only saying this because I want you to do well...

752
49:26.813 --> 49:29.799
That temper of his...

753
49:30.504 --> 49:32.295
Seriously...

754
49:32.295 --> 49:34.010
Beats me.

755
49:34.748 --> 49:36.900
Darn it!

756
49:54.072 --> 49:55.398
[Coach Jang]

757
50:05.855 --> 50:08.125
Once you've looked it all over, give it one final check.

758
50:08.125 --> 50:09.543
Check the schedule too.

759
50:09.543 --> 50:11.781
- Yeah. - In this scene...

760
50:16.392 --> 50:18.069
I'm Jang Jeong Ho, the judo team coach.

761
50:18.069 --> 50:20.574
Who's in charge here?

762
50:21.271 --> 50:23.577
That's me. What is this about?

763
50:23.577 --> 50:24.766
What is this about?

764
50:24.766 --> 50:26.768
You have to ask?

765
50:26.768 --> 50:28.145
Is this about Lee Hyeong Won?

766
50:28.145 --> 50:29.605
Yes, right.

767
50:29.605 --> 50:32.024
You know he's on Korea's national judo team, right?

768
50:32.024 --> 50:33.170
Yes, I do.

769
50:33.170 --> 50:35.694
He chose to audition himself,

770
50:35.694 --> 50:39.831
and I understand the four-day shoot falls during his official leave.

771
50:39.831 --> 50:40.832
Ma'am.

772
50:40.832 --> 50:44.202
We'll be one month out from an international competition.

773
50:44.202 --> 50:46.079
He'll be cutting kilos every day

774
50:46.079 --> 50:50.542
and watching every move to avoid injury in training.

775
50:50.542 --> 50:52.836
We also plan to make sure the shoot doesn't strain him...

776
50:52.836 --> 50:54.838
Those four days...

777
50:54.838 --> 50:56.673
could erase ten years of work

778
50:56.673 --> 50:58.934
and cost Korea a gold medal.

779
50:58.934 --> 51:01.392
That's what I'm telling you!

780
51:01.392 --> 51:02.414
Ma'am.

781
51:02.414 --> 51:05.443
Can you take responsibility for his life?

782
51:12.564 --> 51:14.339
President?

783
51:15.020 --> 51:16.674
Professor Min.

784
51:17.491 --> 51:18.882
Let's keep this short.

785
51:18.882 --> 51:21.691
Get Lee Hyeong Won back immediately.

786
51:31.042 --> 51:33.008
I'm truly sorry.

787
51:35.477 --> 51:37.298
It can't be helped.

788
51:55.958 --> 51:58.701
Is this all of it?

789
51:58.701 --> 51:59.820
Yeah.

790
51:59.820 --> 52:01.780
Sponsors sent it for Hyeong Won.

791
52:01.780 --> 52:03.281
Now it's a goodbye gift.

792
52:03.281 --> 52:05.283
They only sent tiny stuff.

793
52:05.283 --> 52:07.810
You're mad you can't eat it now. Right?

794
52:08.412 --> 52:10.171
We're about to shoot.

795
52:10.171 --> 52:12.499
What good is any of this sponsorship stuff now?

796
52:12.499 --> 52:13.842
That jerk...

797
52:13.842 --> 52:16.962
His judo matters, but our movie's a joke?

798
52:16.962 --> 52:18.380
I never liked him either.

799
52:18.380 --> 52:20.257
He's just so unlikeable.

800
52:20.257 --> 52:21.892
He wasn't treating it like a joke.

801
52:21.892 --> 52:23.106
He was serious about it.

802
52:23.106 --> 52:25.679
That's why he's genuinely sorry.

803
52:25.679 --> 52:27.814
He must be crushed.

804
52:27.814 --> 52:30.219
Thinking about how upset Hyeong Won must be

805
52:30.219 --> 52:32.457
makes me feel even worse.

806
52:33.603 --> 52:35.354
It was ridiculous from the start.

807
52:35.354 --> 52:38.817
Casting a national team athlete right before training camp?

808
52:38.817 --> 52:42.243
I got blinded by the buzz. My bad.

809
52:44.972 --> 52:46.207
Wait.

810
52:46.207 --> 52:49.314
This is sudden, but isn't it actually good?

811
52:49.314 --> 52:52.494
The guy who swooped in is out of the picture. Then...

812
52:52.494 --> 52:54.713
So what are you going to do?

813
52:55.709 --> 52:57.399
Jung Woo Jae...

814
52:57.986 --> 53:00.319
Shouldn't we call him before it's too late?

815
53:01.650 --> 53:03.550
Yeah. Right.

816
53:03.550 --> 53:05.128
Jung Woo Jae.

817
53:05.128 --> 53:07.846
The ideal choice is now a reality.

818
53:07.846 --> 53:09.468
Jung Woo Jae...

819
53:11.349 --> 53:13.675
Should I call him right now?

820
53:13.675 --> 53:14.916
Yeah.

821
53:21.623 --> 53:22.981
Here.

822
53:22.981 --> 53:25.694
- Please confirm this. - The schedule...

823
53:32.334 --> 53:33.823
Gosh...

824
53:34.461 --> 53:36.153
Woo Jae. Over here!

825
53:43.298 --> 53:44.716
Thank God.

826
53:44.716 --> 53:47.511
Sorry for the short notice. Thanks for coming.

827
53:47.511 --> 53:48.804
It's okay.

828
53:48.804 --> 53:51.097
But we start shooting right away,

829
53:51.097 --> 53:53.725
so you'll need to practice pretty hard.

830
53:53.725 --> 53:56.144
Okay. I'll work hard.

831
53:56.144 --> 53:59.350
Don't worry. I'll practice with him myself.

832
53:59.350 --> 54:00.793
Trust me.

833
54:01.743 --> 54:04.152
Work with him as you did with Hyeong Won.

834
54:04.152 --> 54:06.346
I'll do my part, too.

835
54:06.346 --> 54:08.232
Looking forward to working with you.

836
54:09.651 --> 54:11.536
Let's give him a hand!

837
54:11.536 --> 54:13.622
Looking forward to working with you.

838
54:17.958 --> 54:19.251
Let's try it.

839
54:19.251 --> 54:21.610
Ready, action.

840
54:24.631 --> 54:25.853
Cut.

841
54:28.885 --> 54:30.637
So when So Hee walks this way,

842
54:30.637 --> 54:32.350
Gang Ho is standing completely still,

843
54:32.350 --> 54:34.349
which feels a little stiff and unnatural.

844
54:34.349 --> 54:36.393
Angle your body toward her as she passes.

845
54:36.393 --> 54:37.602
Not that way. This way.

846
54:37.602 --> 54:39.980
Turn your body toward where she's going.

847
54:39.980 --> 54:42.533
- Got it. - Loosen up a little.

848
54:45.786 --> 54:47.309
Ready.

849
54:47.996 --> 54:49.313
Action.

850
54:51.983 --> 54:54.160
You don't have to look at me like that.

851
54:54.160 --> 54:56.171
"This was the only place."

852
54:56.171 --> 54:58.498
Let's work on your diction.

853
54:58.498 --> 55:01.251
"This was the only place."

854
55:01.251 --> 55:04.256
"This was the only pla..."

855
55:04.256 --> 55:06.616
- "Place." - "Place."

856
55:06.616 --> 55:08.976
- Try it with a pen in your mouth. - Okay.

857
55:11.469 --> 55:14.598
"This was the only place."

858
55:14.598 --> 55:16.762
"This was the only place."

859
55:18.839 --> 55:20.329
"This was the only place."

860
55:20.329 --> 55:21.813
Better, right?

861
55:21.813 --> 55:22.973
Yeah.

862
55:26.484 --> 55:29.121
"This was the only place."

863
55:42.669 --> 55:45.255
Look. My face is covered, right?

864
55:45.255 --> 55:47.532
Hold it like this.

865
55:47.532 --> 55:49.418
Now my face shows, right?

866
55:50.096 --> 55:51.559
Like this.

867
55:57.474 --> 55:59.357
Want to try another scene?

868
56:31.234 --> 56:33.051
You're good.

869
56:33.051 --> 56:34.260
Thanks.

870
56:34.260 --> 56:35.861
This is hard.

871
57:46.416 --> 57:47.395
Jung Woo Jae.

872
57:47.395 --> 57:48.084
Yeah?

873
57:48.084 --> 57:49.855
What's your dream?

874
57:51.297 --> 57:52.881
A judo player.

875
57:52.881 --> 57:55.258
Maybe I'll make the national team someday.

876
57:55.258 --> 57:58.009
Come on. It's not the end of the world.

877
57:58.009 --> 58:00.847
You can't do judo anymore. So what? Is your life over?

878
58:00.847 --> 58:04.059
I'm not good at anything anymore.

879
58:04.059 --> 58:06.317
Sure you are.

880
58:10.023 --> 58:12.025
Protect me.

881
58:12.025 --> 58:13.916
You can protect me.

882
59:52.011 --> 59:54.393
I'm so scared, Ha Ru.

883
59:56.171 --> 59:59.231
What if I lose Woo Jae all over again?

884
01:00:00.216 --> 01:00:02.385
I'm so scared.

885
01:00:02.385 --> 01:00:03.678
This time is different.

886
01:00:03.678 --> 01:00:06.524
We can save him.

887
01:00:29.454 --> 01:00:31.137
- Shall we go? - Yeah.

888
01:00:33.650 --> 01:00:36.085
We'll have a little time when we get to the location.

889
01:00:36.085 --> 01:00:37.879
Let's run it once more then.

890
01:00:37.879 --> 01:00:40.050
You must be tired from being up all night.

891
01:00:40.050 --> 01:00:42.050
I'm fine. I'll sleep in the car.

892
01:00:56.356 --> 01:00:58.316
Lee Hyeong Won.

893
01:00:58.316 --> 01:01:00.443
I heard you're not doing the movie.

894
01:01:00.443 --> 01:01:02.616
Good call.

895
01:01:03.529 --> 01:01:05.657
You bastard, learn to say hello.

896
01:01:05.657 --> 01:01:08.545
Manners are half of...

897
01:01:22.450 --> 01:01:23.687
Hey.

898
01:01:26.052 --> 01:01:28.139
What is this?

899
01:01:28.139 --> 01:01:29.681
All right. Ready.

900
01:01:29.681 --> 01:01:30.765
Camera rolling!

901
01:01:30.765 --> 01:01:32.987
- Scene... - Take four.

902
01:01:35.254 --> 01:01:36.680
Action.

903
01:02:19.785 --> 01:02:21.267
- What? - Oh my!

904
01:02:21.267 --> 01:02:23.644
Cut! Rain! Cover everything!

905
01:02:24.313 --> 01:02:25.653
Camera! Camera!

906
01:02:25.653 --> 01:02:27.173
What the...

907
01:02:28.086 --> 01:02:29.391
Hey.

908
01:02:29.391 --> 01:02:30.700
What do we do?

909
01:02:30.700 --> 01:02:32.168
It's pouring.

910
01:02:32.168 --> 01:02:33.987
But we have to finish today.

911
01:02:33.987 --> 01:02:35.416
Wait.

912
01:02:36.355 --> 01:02:38.476
- Let's sit over there. - Yeah.

913
01:02:41.430 --> 01:02:43.442
This is insane.

914
01:02:43.442 --> 01:02:45.256
Might just be a shower.

915
01:02:45.256 --> 01:02:46.799
- Bi Gyeong! - Yes?

916
01:02:46.799 --> 01:02:49.209
- 131. - One second.

917
01:02:49.997 --> 01:02:53.212
We need to get this much shot now so we can make up time later.

918
01:02:53.212 --> 01:02:55.016
Weather service?

919
01:02:55.016 --> 01:02:57.185
We're in Unsan-myeon, Haesol City.

920
01:02:57.185 --> 01:03:00.683
Your radar showed no rain clouds today,

921
01:03:00.683 --> 01:03:02.982
but it's pouring here right now.

922
01:03:02.982 --> 01:03:04.711
When will it stop?

923
01:03:05.302 --> 01:03:06.487
Sorry?

924
01:03:07.360 --> 01:03:09.604
Okay, got it.

925
01:03:10.301 --> 01:03:11.574
What'd they say?

926
01:03:11.574 --> 01:03:14.473
They don't know when it'll stop.

927
01:03:14.473 --> 01:03:16.079
What do we do?

928
01:03:16.079 --> 01:03:17.518
Let's go back to base camp.

929
01:03:17.518 --> 01:03:18.859
- Okay. - Yeah.

930
01:03:18.859 --> 01:03:21.503
Everyone, we're heading back to base camp!

931
01:03:23.091 --> 01:03:25.215
[Beast]

932
01:03:25.215 --> 01:03:27.009
[Missed call]

933
01:03:31.928 --> 01:03:33.346
Are you cold?

934
01:03:33.346 --> 01:03:35.215
No, I'm okay.

935
01:03:36.345 --> 01:03:39.560
Guys, everything's packed. We need to go.

936
01:03:39.560 --> 01:03:40.826
Okay.

937
01:03:43.856 --> 01:03:47.276
Oh, right. I need to talk to Jun Mo.

938
01:03:47.276 --> 01:03:49.904
I'll go ahead. Take your time.

939
01:03:49.904 --> 01:03:51.282
- Okay. - Okay.

940
01:04:00.957 --> 01:04:02.417
Actually...

941
01:04:02.417 --> 01:04:06.473
I was kind of glad it started raining earlier.

942
01:04:06.473 --> 01:04:07.855
Why?

943
01:04:09.090 --> 01:04:12.051
I was fine when it was just us practicing,

944
01:04:12.051 --> 01:04:14.470
but doing it with everyone watching...

945
01:04:14.470 --> 01:04:16.889
I got nervous and embarrassed.

946
01:04:16.889 --> 01:04:19.225
My mind went totally blank.

947
01:04:19.225 --> 01:04:20.749
Everyone's like that at first.

948
01:04:20.749 --> 01:04:23.271
But you didn't look flustered at all.

949
01:04:23.271 --> 01:04:25.273
Maybe acting suits you.

950
01:04:25.273 --> 01:04:26.972
Oh, come on.

951
01:04:30.060 --> 01:04:31.863
But...

952
01:04:31.863 --> 01:04:35.575
If I do become an actor, I can't avoid those scenes, can I?

953
01:04:35.575 --> 01:04:36.576
What scenes?

954
01:04:36.576 --> 01:04:38.842
I mean...

955
01:04:38.842 --> 01:04:43.948
I can't only take roles where I don't touch anyone...

956
01:04:43.948 --> 01:04:46.085
- Can I? - Why?

957
01:04:46.085 --> 01:04:50.266
Worried I'd get jealous if you kissed another actress on screen?

958
01:04:51.257 --> 01:04:52.925
No.

959
01:04:52.925 --> 01:04:56.087
I'm worried I'd get jealous.

960
01:04:56.684 --> 01:04:57.805
Jeez.

961
01:04:57.805 --> 01:05:00.369
Why would you be jealous?

962
01:05:01.726 --> 01:05:03.853
I'll try to be okay with it.

963
01:05:03.853 --> 01:05:06.713
No promises, though.

964
01:05:07.469 --> 01:05:08.680
What?

965
01:05:10.026 --> 01:05:14.085
My girlfriend kissing another guy...

966
